  "worked_solution": "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=8\\text{i}$ is a root, its conjugate $x=-8\\text{i}$ must also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-8\\text{i})(x+8\\text{i})=0\n$$\n\nMultiplying out the parentheses and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{(8\\text{i})}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-64(-1) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+64 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
